Package: BKwG
Type: Package
Title: The Beta Kumaraswamy-G Family of Distributions
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-11-06
Authors@R: person("Mohamad Yamen", "AL Mohamad",
    email = "yamenmohamad@tabrizu.ac.ir", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4658-9095"))
Description: A complete toolbox for the beta Kumaraswamy-G (BKw-G) family of
    distributions of Handique, Chakraborty and Ali (2017)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1603.00634>, with cumulative distribution function
    F(x) = I_{1-[1-G(x)^a]^b}(alpha, beta). It provides density, distribution,
    quantile, survival, hazard, cumulative hazard and random generation
    functions for twelve built-in baseline distributions G or any
    user-supplied baseline; the analytical score vector; the nested
    sub-models (Kumaraswamy-G, beta-G, exponentiated Kumaraswamy-G, beta
    exponentiated-G, exponentiated-G and G itself); estimation by maximum
    likelihood, maximum product of spacings, minimum Anderson-Darling and
    Cramer-von Mises distances, ordinary and weighted least squares;
    likelihood ratio and Wald tests; goodness-of-fit statistics
    (Cramer-von Mises W*, Anderson-Darling A*, Kolmogorov-Smirnov) with
    parametric bootstrap p-values; model comparison tables (AIC, CAIC, BIC,
    HQIC); moments, generating function, entropies, mean residual life,
    order statistics and the infinite-mixture representation of the family.
